 61  ;total number of comment lines until data start
;TOTAL SOLAR IRRADIANCE (TSI) DATA FROM VIRGO/SOHO
;This dataset is freely available with one restriction:
;If you use the data or some product based on the data in a published 
;paper refer to one of the publications and acknowlege receipt of the 
;dataset (mention version used) from VIRGO Team through PMOD/WRC, Davos,
;Switzerland, and acknowledge "unpublished data from the VIRGO Experiment 
;on the cooperative ESA/NASA Mission SoHO"
;The data are available from the ftp server ftp.pmodwrc.ch in the directory 
;/data/irradiance/virgo/TSI/virgo_tsi_d_ and virgo_tsi_h_6_001_0607.dat
;for daily and hourly values respectively. 
;The time series VIRGO, DIARAD and PMO6-V are at level 2.0 as determined by 
;comparison of DIARAD and PMO6-V measurements which are first corrected for 
;exposure dependent changes by comparison with the less exposed backup 
;radiometers of each type, called level 1.8 data. The method and procedures 
;are described in Ref2 and 3 and on the VIRGO data home page: 
;     http://www.pmodwrc.ch/pmod.php?topic=tsi/virgo/proj_space_virgo. 
;Independently determined DIARAD data (as described in Ref4) are available from
;     http://remotesensing.oma.be/solarconstant/virgo/diarad_data.htm
;
;   Since version 3.00 a new determination of the degradation of the
;   radiometers has been used to produce level 1.8 and 2.0. 
;   Since version 6.00 the exposure dependent changes of PMO6V have been revised
;   as well as the corresponding non-exposure dependent changes of DIARAD. The internal
;   consistency of the corrections has been improved substantially.
;
;Selected REFERENCES:
;(1)   Fr{\"o}hlich, C., Crommelynck, D., Wehrli, C., Anklin, M., Dewitte, S., Fichot,
;      A., Finsterle, W., Jim{\e}nez, A., Chevalier, A. and Roth, H.~J.,
;      In-flight performances of {VIRGO} solar irradiance instruments on {SOHO},
;      {\em Sol. Phys.} {\bf 175}, p. 267--286., 1997
;(2)   Fr{\"o}hlich, C. and W. Finsterle, `VIRGO Radiometry and Total Solar 
;      Irradiance 1996-2000 Revised. In: P. Brekke, B. Fleck, and J. B. Gurman (eds.): 
;      Recent Insights Into the Physics of the Sun and Heliosphere - Highlights
;      from SOHO and Other Space Missions. p.105-110, ASP Conference Series, 
;      Vol. 203, 2001
;(3)   Fr{\"o}hlich, C., `Long-term Behaviour of Space Radiometers
;      {\em Metrologia}, {\bf 40}, p.60-65, 2003
;(4)   Crommelynck, D., S. Dewitteand A. Joukoff, Total Solar Irradiance 
;      observations from DIARAD/VIRGO, {\em J.Geoph.Res.}, {\bf 109}, 
;      doi: 10.1029/2002JA009694, 2004
;   These publications or preprints of them can be found on the anonymous ftp 
;   server ftp.pmodwrc.ch in the directory /publications/ best reachable 
;   through www.pmodwrc.ch.
;
;Describtion of columns:
;1st col: Date (YYYYMMDD) at noon
;2nd col: TSI VIRGO (Wm-2)
;3rd col: TSI DIARAD level 2 (Wm-2)
;4th col: TSI PMO6-V level 2 (Wm-2)
;5th col: TSI DIARAD level 1.8 (Wm-2)
;6th col: TSI PMO6-V level 1.8 (Wm-2)
;7th col: TSI DIARAD/IRMB (Wm-2)
;format (i4,2i2.2,6f11.5)
;Col 2-7 contain the daily average of the corresponding day.
;Missing values are indicated by -99.
;File created Jul 18 2006
;Version: 6_001_0607
the first part is version of the procedure 
;    and the second part the YYMM month of the update
;                   level 2.0                  level 1.8
;$          VIRGO     DIARAD     PMO6V      DIARAD     PMO6V    DIARAD/IRMB
